        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pomeranian, Sporting Lucas Terrier, Japanese Spitz\n- Concepts: Spitz type, terrier type, breed size standards, Pomerania region\n\nFacts:\n- The Pomeranian, also called a Pom or Pom Pom, is a dog breed of the Spitz type.\n- The Pomeranian is named after the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\n- The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small dog breed of the terrier type.\n- The Japanese Spitz has varying ideal size standards around the world.\n- The Japanese Spitz is always larger than the smaller Pomeranian.",
